igned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c323ef1fed74d1acacb1fab4011c663923b6a74751cbc3bc72ea57d81f81b951"} {"question" "q-317342" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317342" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "52"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $det(Z)$, if\n $Z=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x} & y \\\\ {y}^{2} & \\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(Z) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x} & y \\\\ {y}^{2} & \\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}-y\\cdot {y}^{2} \\\\  & =x-{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c323ef1fed74d1acacb1fab4011c663923b6a74751cbc3bc72ea57d81f81b951"} {"question" "q-1089" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1089" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{x}-{y}^{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{x}-2{y}^{3}"] ["math" "x-2{y}^{2}"] ["math" "x-{y}^{2}"] ["math" "x-{y}^{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1089" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-{y}^{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the determinant:\n\n$|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}|=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}| & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}-y\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c323ef1fed74d1acacb1fab4011c663923b6a74751cbc3bc72ea57d81f81b951"} {"question" "q-317374" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317374" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-4y"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $det(T)$, if\n    $T=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 17 \\\\ 1 & 10\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 17 \\\\ 1 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10-17\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5-17 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c323ef1fed74d1acacb1fab4011c663923b6a74751cbc3bc72ea57d81f81b951"} {"question" "q-1087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-17"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$|\\begin{aligned}2x & {y}^{2} \\\\ z & -3\\end{aligned}|=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2x & {y}^{2} \\\\ z & -3\\end{aligned}| & =2x\\cdot (-3)-{y}^{2}\\cdot z \\\\  & =-6x-{y}^{2}z\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c323ef1fed74d1acacb1fab4011c663923b6a74751cbc3bc72ea57d81f81b951"} {"question" "q-1083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6x-{y}^{2}z"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6x-{y}^{2}"] ["math" "6x-{y}^{2}z"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-1083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6x-{y}^{2}z"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-69649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$|\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{x} & {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}|=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-69649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{x} & {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}| & =3\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (-\\sqrt{x})-{z}^{2}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =-3x-2y{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-69649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c323ef1fed74d1acacb1fab4011c663923b6a74751cbc3bc72ea57d81f81b951"} {"question" "q-69649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-69649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x-3y{z}^{2}"] ["math" "-3x-2y{z}^{2}"] ["math" "-3x-2{y}^{2}z"] ["math" "2x+3y{z}^{2}"] ["math" "3x-2{z}^{2}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-69649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3x-2y{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n    $D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$\\text{det}(D)=-11,$ determine the value of $m.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5-m\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =10-3m.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-11,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-11 \\\\ 10-3m & =-11 \\\\ -3m & =-21 \\\\ m & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c323ef1fed74d1acacb1fab4011c663923b6a74751cbc3bc72ea57d81f81b951"} {"question" "q-317377" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317377" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-127609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3y & y \\\\ 3 & y-5\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(A)=-27$, what is the value of $y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-127609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3y & y \\\\ 3 & y-5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3y\\cdot (y-5)-y\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-18y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=-27$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y+27 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y+9 & =0 \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-127609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c323ef1fed74d1acacb1fab4011c663923b6a74751cbc3bc72ea57d81f81b951"} {"question" "q-127609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-127609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-9"] ["math" "y=18"] ["math" "y=3"] ["math" "y=\\frac{18}{2}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-127609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-127608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}5-p & p \\\\ 3 & p\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(B)=1$, what is the value of $p?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-127608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}5-p & p \\\\ 3 & p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5-p)\\cdot p-p\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-{p}^{2}+2p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(B)=1$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1 \\\\ -{p}^{2}+2p & =1 \\\\ -{p}^{2}+2p-1 & =0 \\\\ {p}^{2}-2p+1 & =0 \\\\ (p-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-127608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c323ef1fed74d1acacb1fab4011c663923b6a74751cbc3bc72ea57d81f81b951"} {"question" "q-127608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-127608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "p=-5"] ["math" "p=1"] ["math" "p=3"] ["math" "p=\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "p=\\frac{2}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-127608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "p=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n$U=[\\begin{aligned}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(U)=-6$, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =|\\begin{aligned}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1+r)\\cdot 4-(2-r)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =4+4r+10-5r \\\\  & =14-r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-6 \\\\ 14-r & =-6 \\\\ -r & =-20 \\\\ r & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c323ef1fed74d1acacb1fab4011c663923b6a74751cbc3bc72ea57d81f81b951"} {"question" "q-317382" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317382" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(S)=25,$ what is the value of $s?$\n\n$s=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3+s)(3-s)-2s(-4) \\\\  & =9-{s}^{2}+8s \\\\  & =-{s}^{2}+8s+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s+9 & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s-16 & =0 \\\\ {s}^{2}-8s+16 & =0 \\\\ (s-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ s & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c323ef1fed74d1acacb1fab4011c663923b6a74751cbc3bc72ea57d81f81b951"} {"question" "q-317385" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "q-317385" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/state.json" "file_sha256" "464a9853726e71fd3fbc4bba1d41431ea1a32d0ba724fb022afe59bcff3a67cf"} {"question" "e-4434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\det(A),$ if $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/example-4434.json" "file_sha256" "06aa87e0bdbf31f57fde1658642692e2914c410562e1af03d2e487aee38a42b7"} {"question" "e-4434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =18-10 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/example-4434.json" "file_sha256" "06aa87e0bdbf31f57fde1658642692e2914c410562e1af03d2e487aee38a42b7"} {"question" "e-4435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\det(A),$ if $[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/example-4435.json" "file_sha256" "078ab228deddba5c1e5f774e89c246cef4fe71b970db38a70ef2392712990272"} {"question" "e-4435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}-(-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/example-4435.json" "file_sha256" "078ab228deddba5c1e5f774e89c246cef4fe71b970db38a70ef2392712990272"} {"question" "e-4436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n${A} = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        2 & -1 \\\n        -3 & k\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack$\nand\n$\\det({A}) = 5$, what is the value of $k?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/example-4436.json" "file_sha256" "36c1ea8cc4d16dba791ce38c30e80527077c2bce4fff3669dab0cbeb1471b057"} {"question" "e-4436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot k-(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =2k-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=5,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =5 \\\\ 2k-3 & =5 \\\\ 2k & =8 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035974/example-4436.json" "file_sha256" "36c1ea8cc4d16dba791ce38c30e80527077c2bce4fff3669dab0cbeb1471b057"}] "usage" {"q-1080" [] "q-1089" [] "q-317374" [] "q-1079" [] "q-317335" [] "e-4435" [] "e-4434" [] "e-4436" []} "basis" 1240 "retractions" [[17592186059904 :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$, if\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186059906 :question/problem "Calculate $det(Z)$, if\n\n$Z = \\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{x} & y \\\\ y^{2} & \\sqrt{x}\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186059481 :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A)$, if $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186059481 :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 6 - 2 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&= 18 - 10 \\\\\n&= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059482 :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A)$, if $\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186059482 :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= \\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} - (-2) \\cdot 0 \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059483 :question/problem "If\n${A} = \\left\\lbrack \\matrix {2 & -1 \\ -3 & k} \\right\\rbrack$\nand\n$\\det({A}) = 5$, what is the value of $k$?"] [17592186059483 :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot k - (-1) \\cdot (-3) \\\\\n&= 2k - 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=5$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= 5 \\\\\n2k - 3 &= 5 \\\\\n2k &= 8 \\\\\nk &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186056144 17592186056145 17592186056146 17592186056147 17592186056148 17592186056156 17592186056157 17592186056158 17592186056159 17592186056160 17592186264422 17592186264423 17592186264424 17592186264425 17592186264426 17592186264475 17592186264476 17592186275857] "immutable_fields" [[17592186056143 :answer-field/correct] [17592186056143 :answer-field/id] [17592186056143 :answer-field/key] [17592186056143 :answer-field/type] [17592186056155 :answer-field/correct] [17592186056155 :answer-field/id] [17592186056155 :answer-field/key] [17592186056155 :answer-field/type] [17592186264421 :answer-field/correct] [17592186264421 :answer-field/id] [17592186264421 :answer-field/key] [17592186264421 :answer-field/type] [17592186264474 :answer-field/correct] [17592186264474 :answer-field/id] [17592186264474 :answer-field/key] [17592186264474 :answer-field/type] [17592186275856 :answer-field/correct] [17592186275856 :answer-field/id] [17592186275856 :answer-field/key] [17592186275856 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
